>Okay, so how do we distinguish "Everything is white if it's a swan" from 
>"If
>everything is a swan, then something is white"?

The former is:

  ganai roda nebdatka gi da blabi

The latter:

  ganai roda nebdatka gi [su'o]de blabi

There is no implicit {su'o} in the first case,
because {da} is already bound.

